thig6.7:1.1 starts: [The Buddha admonished me:]
# superseded: thig6.7:1.2 starts: devote yourself to the goal
thig6.7:1.3 starts: having discarded [hope]
thig6.7:1.4 starts: Don’t fall under the sway
thig6.7:2.1 starts: Hoodwinked by mind,
thig6.7:2.2 starts: beings in love with Māra’s realm,
thig6.7:2.3 starts: roam
thig6.7:2.4 starts: through the many-birth wandering-on,
thig7.2:1.1 starts: Cālā:
thig7.2:1.2 starts: a nun with developed faculties,
thig7.2:1.3 starts: I
thig7.2:1.4 starts: stilling-of-fabrications bliss.
thig7.3:1.1 starts: Upacālā:
thig7.3:1.2 starts: a nun with developed faculties,
thig7.3:1.3 starts: I
thig7.3:1.4 starts: of which worthless people
thig7.3:3.1 starts: Upacālā:
thig7.3:3.2 starts: the cutting-off of hands & feet,
thig7.3:3.3 starts: binding, flogging, torment.
thig7.3:3.4 starts: One who’s born incurs pain.
thig7.3:4.1 starts: But there is
thig7.3:4.2 starts: the undefeated one,
thig7.3:4.3 starts: He taught me the Dhamma
thig7.3:4.4 starts: for the transcending of birth:
thig8.1:6.1 starts: The unshaken, incomparable
thig8.1:6.2 starts: —the Dhamma the Buddha taught to me,
thig8.1:6.3 starts: of which people run-of-the-mill
thig8.1:6.4 starts: that’s where my heart
thig9.1:4.1 starts: Vaḍḍha:
thig9.1:4.2 starts: you speak this matter to me.
thig9.1:4.3 starts: I suspect that now in you
thig9.1:4.4 starts: no underbrush
thig9.1:5.1 starts: Vaḍḍha’s Mother:
thig9.1:5.2 starts: are lowly, middling, or exalted:
thig9.1:5.3 starts: No underbrush for them in me
thig9.1:5.4 starts: —not a bit, not the least little bit—
